  "summary": "Package exfiltrates host identifiers to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint on install and require",
  "details": "The package exists solely to execute a beacon. package.json declares scripts.postinstall = \"node beacon.cjs\", and index.js exports a Proxy of no-op functions whose only side effect on require is invoking require('./beacon.cjs').fire(). beacon.cjs collects host identifiers — os.hostname(), __dirname, process.cwd(), process.version, and the package name — and POSTs them to the hardcoded plain-HTTP bare-IP endpoint http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc. The destination is unrelated to any publisher domain, the behavior fires both at install time (postinstall) and on module load, and the package has no legitimate functionality beyond this beacon.",
